note 10 the typed text as a web address (0 it is none, 1 written with its scheme, 2 a bare address) 12 where the
note typed text starts once blanks are trimmed 13 its length then 14 1 when the program stays (no HOPCHECK)
note 15 what registering the hot key gave (0 it is registered) 16 the words of the typed text 17 the files found
note 18 1 when a file has exactly the typed text as its name 19 bytes of the answer waiting in g_net
note 20 1 when an answer is on show 21 1 when the model's answer has ended 22 1 when a piece of it came
note 23 1 when the check asks for what is chosen to be remembered without being opened 24 the count of copied
note things 25 the bytes of the newest one's text when it may be a web address 26 its address kind 27 the count
note of other copied things offered 28 the count of copied things that match the typed text 29 what the check
note pasted (1 text, 2 a picture) 30 the row the check chooses before Enter (0: the first) 31 the count of
note saved accounts 32 the place plus 1 of the app that was in front before the one in front now
note 33 1 once the history was set aside before this run's first change to it 34 how many unpinned copied
note things are kept 35 the clipboard's change count last seen 36 the screen the list shows (0 everything,
note 1 the copied things, 2 the saved accounts) 37 what a check does to the selected copied thing (1 pin or
note unpin, 2 delete) 38 half seconds since the file index was last looked at
note 39 1 when the answer on show belongs to a turn that has ended 40 1 when that turn failed 41 1 when the
note typed text reads as a question 42 1 when Hop's settings send a sentence to the agent on Enter 43 1 while
note the agent runs 44 1 once the person said yes to the agent 45 1 once the agents on this Mac were looked
note for 46 1 when a check sends what it types to the agent 47 what of the agent's run has ended (1 its
note output, 2 the program) 48 the turn at which a check sends Enter 49 the count of files found on other
note machines 50 the bytes of what the machines answered 51 what to say about a machine (1 unreachable, 2 building
note its list, 3 a file is on its way, 4 a path was copied, 5 a file could not be brought) 52 which machine
note 53 the bytes of the text the machines were asked for 54 the count of machines 55 1 when a check's file
note arrived 56 the machine and 57 the found file that is on its way 58 1 when a file found on a machine has exactly the typed name
note 59 1 when other machines may be reached 60 half seconds since the forwarded ports were last looked at
note 61 how many links this program has started 62 how many forwarded ports the settings name
