note ---- forwarded ports: the ssh links Hop keeps open (Sources/Factory.swift, TunnelManager) ----
note Hop's settings name ports of other computers to have on this Mac (a model's server, the factory, the
note knowledge base). At the start and every 20 seconds each one whose link is not running is looked at: when
note nothing on this Mac serves its port (nc is asked, as a program of its own), ssh is started for it with Hop's own options (a link of its own, never
note the shared connection, so it ends cleanly). A port something else serves is left alone, and so Hop and this
note program do not fight over one. When this program quits it ends its links. Not here yet: dropping the links
note at once when the network changes (ssh notices by itself within 45 seconds, and the link is made anew).
note the whole number an object of the settings holds: 0 when it is not a number, is a yes or a no, or is not
note whole (8080.9 is no port, and Hop takes none of these either)
fn uwhole obj ulong to ulong
if not uisnumber obj
ret 0
end
yes_object = uconst s_cf_true
no_object = uconst s_cf_false
if or eq obj yes_object eq obj no_object
ret 0
end
v = umsg obj usl m_integer_value 0 0 0
same_v = umsg ucl c_number usl m_number_integer v 0 0
if eq and umsg obj usl m_is_equal_number same_v 0 0 255 0
ret 0
end
ret v
end

